          "title": "You'll want to know: deswegen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deswegen — \"that is why, for that reason\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ich habe verschlafen. Deswegen bin ich zu spät gekommen. I overslept. That is why I was late."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The verb comes right after it, as after deshalb: deswegen bin ich …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deswegen joins des, the old genitive \"of that\", to wegen \"because of\", which grew from von … wegen \"on the part of\". EtymDB has the word but no history for it."
            }
          ]
        },
